+/// Verity (lane flock-zk, M1): VEIL's hiding for Ligerito's level 0 (ePrint 2026/683 Figs. 8–9; verity's
+/// `backends/flock/live/PROTOCOL.md` §8). Every lane's message is padded by the polynomial `(Ŵ_n + c)·μ` (`μ` of degree
+/// `< t_pad` uniform, `Ŵ_n = X_L` the novel basis's vanishing polynomial of the message subspace, `c` outside GF(2)):
+/// `X_L` alone vanishes on half the codeword's positions, `X_L + c` on none, so any `t_pad` opened positions of a lane are
+/// uniform. Four uniform lanes (padded too) follow the witness's, a pair per repetition: every repetition opens the one
+/// level-0 codeword, and rep `r`'s fold takes only its own pair, `ρ_0 R_{2r} + ρ_1 R_{2r+1}` (`ρ` fresh F256 coins,
+/// F128-independent), so its level 1 commits a uniform table. A pair shared by two reps would leak: their two folds and
+/// two padding combinations eliminate it. Before `ρ` the prover sends the pair's sums `e` against the folded basis (exposed:
+/// masked by the caller's pads; VEIL Fig. 9 step 1), after it the blinded claim `T' = claim + ρ_0 e_0 + ρ_1 e_1` and the
+/// padding's combination `ybar`.
